Solve, algebraically.
\[
e^{2 x-3}=7^{x+1}
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\ln e^{2 x-3} & =\ln 7^{x+1} \\
(2 x-3) \ln e & =(x+1) \ln 7 \\
2 x-3 & =x \ln 7+\ln 7 \\
2 x-x \ln 7 & =\ln 7+3 \\
x(2-\ln 7) & =\ln 7+3 \\
x & =\frac{\ln 7+3}{2-\ln 7} \\
x & =91.438783 \\
x & =91.439
\end{aligned}
\]
