Determine, algebraically, the inverse of \(f(x)=3 x+4\).

\section*{Solution}

Let \(f(x)=y\)
\[
\begin{array}{ll}
y=3 x+4 & \\
x=3 y+4 & 1 \text { mark for switching } x \text { and } y \text {-values } \\
x-4=3 y & \\
\frac{x-4}{3}=y & 1 / 2 \text { mark for solving for } y
\end{array}
\]
\(f^{-1}(x)=\frac{x-4}{3} \quad \frac{1}{2}\) mark for writing equation of \(f^{-1}(x)\)
